feat(console): add REBOOT and FASTBOOT recovery commands

The USB debug console is the only way into a machine whose test loop ends in
a panic, but until now it could only watch.  Two newline-terminated commands
give the host a way to restart the board without touching it:

  REBOOT     requests the platform restart path, PEHaltRestart(kPERestartCPU)
  FASTBOOT   writes the Qualcomm restart_reason cookie in IMEM and then asks
             for the same restart

Both are matched inside one bulk-OUT completion, because the CDC-ACM driver
only sees the bytes of that transfer; a command split across two writes is
not a command.  The panic pump records the request while it owns the
transport and executes it only after ud_leave(), since the restart path
prints through the same console and must be able to flush.  The normal event
thread uses the same deferred path.

A restart requested by the console must not pass through the panic-spin
interception in KebabPlatformExpert::haltRestart(): that would call
kebab_usb_panic_spin() a second time, which refuses a nested spinner and
waits forever.  The driver exports kebab_usb_restart_armed() so the platform
expert can tell the host request apart from a panic stop and let the restart
through.

PEHaltRestart() had no backend on this port: nothing installs
PE_halt_restart, so IODTPlatformExpert::haltRestart() returned -1 without
touching the hardware.  The platform expert now implements kPERestartCPU
with PSCI SYSTEM_RESET, the same firmware interface KebabCPU already uses
for CPU_ON.  That keeps PEHaltRestart as the entry point and avoids a
driver-private reset register.

FASTBOOT maps the IMEM page once at start-up, in normal context, and logs the
old and new restart_reason before writing.  The address and offset come from
the device DTB (qcom,msm-imem@146bf000 / restart_reason@65c).  The cookie
value is a hypothesis, not a measured fact: kebab_fastboot_cookie=<hex>
overrides the default 0x77665501 without a rebuild.  A wrong value can land
the board in recovery or EDL; EDL needs firehose tooling this project does
not have.  If the restart call returns, the old value is restored so a later
manual reset does not inherit an undelivered fastboot request.

